      \field{labelnamesource}{author}
      \field{labeltitlesource}{title}
      \field{abstract}{This paper introduces a new approach for solving the Kepler equation for hyperbolic orbits through the Hyperbolic Kepler Equation--Space Dynamics Group (HKE--SDG) code. Rather than developing new algorithms, we substantially improve classic Newton--Raphson schemes by optimizing the initial seed selection. For discretized domains of hyperbolic anomaly, we implement fifth-degree interpolating polynomials (with asymptotic expansion for the final interval) whose six coefficients are determined by matching function values and first derivatives at interval endpoints. A specialized asymptotic expansion handles the singular corner ($|M| < 0.15$, $1 < e < 1.25$). Numerical simulations demonstrate machine-error accuracy within maximum three iterations (99.8\% cases $\leq$2 iterations) across double/quadruple precision implementations. The HKE--SDG algorithm achieves superior precision (0.3s execution in double precision) while maintaining reliability, particularly in the singular corner where a single asymptotic expansion suffices. Comparative analysis confirms its precision advantage over existing methods in both precision regimes.}
      \field{journaltitle}{Astronomy \& Astrophysics}
      \field{title}{An efficient code to solve the Kepler equation-Hyperbolic case}
